{"parentUuid":"4492ea29-b730-46cb-9a2d-80112fd7a75c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"60f4c23f-cf99-4939-be71-3273a059619c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N6G2HoEvGJFGf61AVLQC68","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough now to compile findings. Note `hasPendingV2FullGenerationPublications` opens a repo + reads pending file, and then `pushV2RefsWithRecovery` → `publishPendingV2FullGenerationPublications` opens the repo again and re-reads the same pending file. Also `gitCommonDir` shells out for every read/write/lock acquisition.\n\n# Efficiency findings\n\n## Notable issues\n\n**1. `gitCommonDir` shells out to `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` on every pending-file operation** — `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_pending_rotation.go:219-242`\n\n`pendingFullGenerationPublicationFilePath` and `pendingFullGenerationPublicationLockPath` both call `gitCommonDir`, and each lock-protected operation calls them at least twice (once for the lock path, once for the file path inside the callback's read/write). A single rotation triggers `Append` (2× exec for lock+file path, plus another for write), and on the next push `publishPendingV2FullGenerationPublications` reads it again, then `RemovePendingFullGenerationPublications` reads + writes again. Each one forks `git`. The common-dir is invariant for a `V2GitStore` — cache it on the store (`s.commonDir`) once and reuse. Worst case a rotation+push currently does ~6 `git rev-parse` invocations where 1 would suffice.\n\n**2. Pending file is read twice on every push when there are pending publications** — `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/push_v2.go:741-794`\n\n`pushV2Refs` calls `hasPendingV2FullGenerationPublications` (which opens the repo, builds a `V2GitStore`, and `ReadPendingFullGenerationPublications` reads + parses the JSON), then calls `pushV2RefsWithRecovery` → `publishPendingV2FullGenerationPublications`, which immediately repeats all three: `OpenRepository`, `NewV2Git