{"parentUuid":"dd02821e-e7da-4cf6-bb1f-91efd3ccb520","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"60f4c23f-cf99-4939-be71-3273a059619c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ANyKEgnQFjeWXcRuTCC7hZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tpackage checkpoint\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"context\"\n5\t\t\"fmt\"\n6\t\n7\t\t\"github.com/go-git/go-git/v6\"\n8\t\t\"github.com/go-git/go-git/v6/plumbing\"\n9\t\t\"github.com/go-git/go-git/v6/plumbing/object\"\n10\t)\n11\t\n12\t// V2GitStore provides checkpoint storage operations for the v2 ref layout.\n13\t// It writes to two custom refs under refs/entire/:\n14\t//   - /main: permanent metadata + compact transcripts\n15\t//   - /full/current: active generation of raw transcripts\n16\t//\n17\t// V2GitStore is separate from GitStore (v1) to keep concerns isolated\n18\t// and simplify future v1 removal. It composes GitStore internally to\n19\t// reuse ref-agnostic entry-building helpers (tree surgery, session\n20\t// indexing, summary aggregation).\n21\ttype V2GitStore struct {\n22\t\trepo *git.Repository\n23\t\tgs   *GitStore // shared entry-building helpers (same package)\n24\t\n25\t\t// maxCheckpointsPerGeneration overrides the rotation threshold for testing.\n26\t\t// Zero means use DefaultMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration.\n27\t\tmaxCheckpointsPerGeneration int\n28\t\n29\t\t// FetchRemote is the git remote used for fetch-on-demand operations (e.g.,\n30\t\t// fetching /full/* refs during entire resume). Defaults to \"origin\".\n31\t\t// Set to the checkpoint remote URL when checkpoint_remote is configured.\n32\t\tFetchRemote string\n33\t\n34\t\t// blobFetcher fetches missing blobs by hash. When set, read paths wrap\n35\t\t// trees with FetchingTree so missing blobs are auto-recovered (and the\n36\t\t// cat-file fallback covers partial-clone-filtered blobs that go-git's\n37\t\t// storer can't see).\n38\t\tblobFetcher BlobFetchFunc\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\t// maxCheckpoints returns the effective rotation threshold.\n42\tfunc